Kamski Playtest | PATCH 0.0.1 - "UI rework & small quality of life improvements" is now LIVE!
[hr][/hr]
📋Full Patch Notes
[hr][/hr]
User Interface
 Fire balls shot from enemies are now red to distinguish them from player shot fire balls
 Added a health bar so it's easier to see your health now
 Items now display their abilities if they provide one
 Added a dynamic hotbar to show which ability is equipped in which slot
 Added a pop-up to settings menu in case user forgets to save the settings
 Changed the look of some user interface elements across the game
 Most user interface elements have an animation now
 Added a second icon for dropped items to better differentiate between the item that gives the fireball ability and the one that gives the dash ability
 Stats are now in a separate window that can be opened with "C"

Other improvements
 You can close settings menu by pressing escape as well
 Movement is changed from traditional "WASD" to Left click. Players can either hold Left click and the character will move towards the mouse pointer or they can click anywhere on the screen and the character will go to that place
 Items can be instantly picked-up with inventory open
 Items can also be picked up when clicked from afar. Character will go towards the item and pick when in range.

[hr][/hr]

We also did some small quality of life improvements and fixes.
[hr][/hr]

You can finally know what ability each item grants you, if any.{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/45293176/4a673da6ffee929ac5dd02160df4e306028a2a2e.png
We also added a hotbar to help the players know which ability is on which slot number.
And a bunch of other changes to the existing UI elements.

Now that steam integration is done, focus was on reworking the UI framework on the engine side for the 4-th and hopefully... last time. With the new UI, we managed to reduce the code needed to make any sort of UI by a factor of 3!
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/45293176/822e9e88e69395bc85fc948de29daae5a9a70204.png

